# Everything this app reads from the environment.
#
# The Supabase variables that used to head this file are gone: the database was
# deleted and the app was rebuilt around Vercel Blob, so listing them here only
# ever sent someone to set up a service nothing reads.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- core
# Writing captions. Every generation run bills against this key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Where captions, ticks, facts, feedback and the image library are stored.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- locks
# The key that lets a request change anything: publish, generate, edit facts,
# write a caption, export the calendar. Reads stay open without it. See
# lib/gate.ts. If neither this nor CRON_SECRET is set, writing is switched off
# rather than left open.
APP_KEY=

# Authorises the two cron routes, and is accepted as a second app key so that
# existing scripts keep working.
CRON_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the 8am email
# Without RESEND_API_KEY the daily route still builds the plan and reports what
# it would have sent, so everything but the last hop can be tested.
RESEND_API_KEY=
DIGEST_TO=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ publishing
# All optional. A brand with no credentials simply isn't connected, the Post
# button doesn't appear for it, and nothing else changes. See /connect in the
# app for what each one is and where to get it, and lib/accounts.ts for the
# naming rule: brand slug, uppercased, hyphens to underscores.
#
# Instagram, per brand — the account must be a Business or Creator account:
#   IG_USER_ID_<SLUG>        the numeric account id, not the @handle
#   IG_TOKEN_<SLUG>          long-lived Instagram Login token (expires in 60 days)
#   META_PAGE_TOKEN_<SLUG>   the older route instead, for an account tied to a Page
#   FB_PAGE_ID_<SLUG>        set alongside META_PAGE_TOKEN to post to the Page too
#
# X — one app covers every brand, then one token pair per account:
#   X_API_KEY=
#   X_API_SECRET=
#   X_ACCESS_TOKEN_<SLUG>
#   X_ACCESS_SECRET_<SLUG>
